From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 16:10:14 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: mediatek: gemini-station: run the eMMC at HS400

At HS200 the station's eMMC reads correct data, but some multi-block
reads fail their data CRC at the tuned read delay, and the block driver
re-reads them a sector at a time, down to a few MB/s. Pad and latch
settings copied from the vendor kernel made it worse.

The vendor kernel never reads data at HS200 on this eMMC. It tunes
HS200 for about 40 ms on the way to HS400, then runs HS400, where the
host samples read data on the card's data strobe rather than a tuned
delay. In every retained vendor boot log of this unit its strobe tuning
ends at DLY1 7 or 8, DLY2 0, DLY3 20.

Allow HS400 at 1.8 V and seed PAD_DS_TUNE with DLY_SEL, DLY1 7 and
DLY3 20 (0x1401d). mtk-sd's HS400 tuning then rescans DLY1 against
EXT_CSD reads. Keep the 64-cell HS200 scan, and correct its comment:
the HS200 window was not above the first 32 cells.

Not yet run on hardware.
---
 .../arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts
index 1f242fd..98acc62 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts
@@ -689,9 +689,13 @@
 	mmc-hs200-1_8v;
 
 	/*
-	 * Scan all 64 delay cells. The data window on this eMMC sits above the
-	 * first 32, and a 32-cell scan centres CMD and DATA near its lower edge.
+	 * HS200 is only the step to HS400 here, as in the vendor kernel. Its
+	 * read delay is marginal on this eMMC; HS400 samples on the card's data
+	 * strobe. The strobe delay is the vendor's (DLY3 20, DLY1 7); mtk-sd
+	 * retunes DLY1 itself. A 64-cell scan gives HS200 tuning a wider window.
 	 */
+	mmc-hs400-1_8v;
+	hs400-ds-delay = <0x1401d>;
 	mediatek,tuning-step = <64>;
 };
 
